{"agent_id":"pp3g-4eBL-clean-room-adversarial-review-on-444-you-are-one-of","agent_seq":1,"timestamp":"2026-08-24T01:48:17.820156858Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"36ca7a67-bf3a-41d3-8648-353118bdde58","comment_uuid":"76c4ad1f-e45c-4d01-97a7-cb98599f9f75","author":"pp3g-4eBL-clean-room-adversarial-review-on-444-you-are-one-of","content":"Plan: Clean-room adversarial review of the continuous log-tail liveness monitor proposal (#443). I have read the shipped current state (scripts/agent-liveness.py v2 + scripts/liveness-watchdog.sh) and the proposal text. I will produce findings as {statement | why-it-matters | cheapest-test | severity} across the mandated attack surfaces (attribution, rotation, tail SPOF, parser brittleness, spiral false-positives, latency, scale, guard interaction, kill trust basis), then post a verdict (adopt/modify/reject+alternative). Read-only; comments only on #444; sync once at end.","created_at":"2026-08-24T01:48:17.813622782Z","kind":"plan","signed_by":"SHA256:usl0k0EVKIRzWIYxQlgcjiM/cGQ8uEjxBXwkMq/YBro","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgCLvCYlub0EX1P/3vBtfMaCQEYV65ygOLwZSOiPTrhK4AAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABASfaX/olsZcJTDOonivbmaoe3mdH4biz2YkCW9D12rEXZJYStcn2pgh/W2yxDJBsIZFFzbFIMvhy3Az7pKA+HBA=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:usl0k0EVKIRzWIYxQlgcjiM/cGQ8uEjxBXwkMq/YBro","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgCLvCYlub0EX1P/3vBtfMaCQEYV65ygOLwZSOiPTrhK4AAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQDROg7o4pOZY2/7y4go5mzo6UyRrFoh+GkVKBvCYbTG7QKZUiSD/ItwaQs1GAMjrYIw5sOlnZfWqz6y4O8xABQc="}
{"agent_id":"pp3g-4eBL-clean-room-adversarial-review-on-444-you-are-one-of","agent_seq":2,"timestamp":"2026-08-24T01:48:42.047119927Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"36ca7a67-bf3a-41d3-8648-353118bdde58","comment_uuid":"aaa2ba56-0e36-476d-a777-d92583d9945d","author":"pp3g-4eBL-clean-room-adversarial-review-on-444-you-are-one-of","content":"[PROGRESS] state=working completed=plan posted next=write findings across attack surfaces then verdict blocker=none","created_at":"2026-08-24T01:48:42.040975082Z","kind":"observation","signed_by":"SHA256:usl0k0EVKIRzWIYxQlgcjiM/cGQ8uEjxBXwkMq/YBro","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgCLvCYlub0EX1P/3vBtfMaCQEYV65ygOLwZSOiPTrhK4AAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABAyBB6xBXPwNajEN+qpSI8a+K2a8PZcNwR6gOtota0HiU9KUb7Tiy9TMLRGNxvBXqRvntrfvjhCVCxF7w9HmCwAA=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:usl0k0EVKIRzWIYxQlgcjiM/cGQ8uEjxBXwkMq/YBro","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgCLvCYlub0EX1P/3vBtfMaCQEYV65ygOLwZSOiPTrhK4AAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQD+lABqFgx1QvTWN2h7VtN37bm63iaaSrCmh5jmr81I470p6kGJZIce9I22X/jGRWI3I/LSig8iS32rCLZbcoAI="}
{"agent_id":"pp3g-4eBL-clean-room-adversarial-review-on-444-you-are-one-of","agent_seq":3,"timestamp":"2026-08-24T01:50:33.040768134Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"36ca7a67-bf3a-41d3-8648-353118bdde58","comment_uuid":"f284eadd-c93e-483a-95b4-e656fc3aa428","author":"pp3g-4eBL-clean-room-adversarial-review-on-444-you-are-one-of","content":"FINDINGS (1/4) — attribution & correlation (BLOCKING)\n\nF1 — Attribution is the load-bearing assumption and is unverified.\n- statement: The whole mechanism attributes each shared-log line to an agent. The proposal itself states 'S2 fork binary writes it, v2 TUI logging behavior unverified' and 'shared single log file needs attribution mapping.' No evidence is offered that the log carries a stable per-agent/session token, nor a mapping to a worktree/agent.\n- why-it-matters: If lines can't be attributed, PARKED-RETRYING/STREAM-DEATH/SPIRAL are misrouted; a misattributed kill hits the WRONG agent; the evidence bundle is also corrupted, defeating audit. Adopt/reject turns on this.\n- cheapest-test: Get one real multi-agent opencode.log from BOTH producers; confirm (a) a per-line session/agent token exists, (b) stable for agent lifetime, (c) maps to a discoverable agent (worktree/.kickoff-metadata). Any failure => design cannot proceed as specified.\n- severity: MUST FIX (blocking).\n\nF2 — STREAM-DEATH request-correlation is unspecified.\n- statement: 'unresolved-request aging past threshold' requires correlating a request-issued event with its resolution for the SAME request. No correlation key (request ID? call UUID? recency heuristic?) is given.\n- why-it-matters: Without it, 'unresolved' is indistinguishable from 'slow but healthy mid-call.' The motivating deepseek case was 'request issued, never resolved, zero errors' — but if no request ID exists, the watcher can't know two lines are one request, so it either never detects death or false-positives on every slow call.\n- cheapest-test: Inspect real logs for a request/call identifier present in both issue and completion lines. If absent, STREAM-DEATH collapses to a last-activity timeout — which the existing poll already does, so eventing adds nothing for this class.\n- severity: MUST FIX (blocking for STREAM-DEATH class).","created_at":"2026-08-24T01:50:33.034115317Z","kind":"observation","signed_by":"SHA256:usl0k0EVKIRzWIYxQlgcjiM/cGQ8uEjxBXwkMq/YBro","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgCLvCYlub0EX1P/3vBtfMaCQEYV65ygOLwZSOiPTrhK4AAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABAjCbtC4RYwEe2jbwCY325F0ZaW7Cdt2c2oa4dusHsZObPprd0y00Qs5yvb3kW0Pnm41amG8GmCz6qBk/phNpxCw=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:usl0k0EVKIRzWIYxQlgcjiM/cGQ8uEjxBXwkMq/YBro","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgCLvCYlub0EX1P/3vBtfMaCQEYV65ygOLwZSOiPTrhK4AAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQCFYburxNx8jVncmytG3G1pYw6i0V39uUJUUWQxM9QcgaBNU78rwcpGfta26Ek4RNzKU8WTVhGo5Nrtg9RA+dg8="}
{"agent_id":"pp3g-4eBL-clean-room-adversarial-review-on-444-you-are-one-of","agent_seq":4,"timestamp":"2026-08-24T01:50:42.045122799Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"36ca7a67-bf3a-41d3-8648-353118bdde58","comment_uuid":"365b460c-5f7f-4a7a-8c87-d5fc2f783777","author":"pp3g-4eBL-clean-room-adversarial-review-on-444-you-are-one-of","content":"FINDINGS (2/4) — parser, spiral false-positives, kill trust (BLOCKING for auto-kill)\n\nF3 — Parser built on one night's inferred strings, not a schema.\n- statement: Keys on 'AI_APICallError'+'retry-after' and 'request issued, never resolved, zero errors' — forensic observations, not a specified contract; v2 TUI behavior admitted unverified.\n- why-it-matters: Real wording varies (RateLimitError, 429, quota_exceeded, upstream connect error, stream closed, context deadline exceeded). A parser matching only observed strings silently misses most real failures — the worst mode for a safety mechanism (false negative = the exact death it was built to catch goes undetected).\n- cheapest-test: Build an error/stream corpus from both producers across failure types; measure parser coverage; add an 'unrecognized-line-rate' alert for schema drift.\n- severity: HIGH (MUST FIX before trusting classifications; acceptable only behind shadow-mode).\n\nF4 — Spiral auto-kill false-positive risk on legitimate verbose tasks.\n- statement: SPIRAL = 'repetition-ratio over trailing window with no fresh commits/checkpoints => automatic kill after one confirmation cycle.' Metric, window, threshold unspecified; only guardrail is 'BOTH high similarity AND no progress signals.'\n- why-it-matters: Asymmetric risk. A false-positive kill destroys an agent's in-progress (possibly uncommitted) work — irreversible. A false-negative only costs tokens and is caught by the poll backstop. The proposal's own deepseek '25-min invisible churn' example is exactly the long repetitive-looking activity that could trip a naive detector yet may be real work. Test-suite output, build warnings, large diffs, code-gen loops routinely emit high-similarity lines >90s without a commit.\n- cheapest-test: Labeled corpus of (a) good verbose runs and (b) real spirals; find a threshold separating them with ~zero false positives on (a); run detector in SHADOW mode (WOULD-KILL, no kill) across real agents for a defined period; count false positives before any kill is authorized.\n- severity: MUST FIX (auto-kill authority should not be granted until shadow-mode false-positive rate is demonstrated near-zero).\n\nF11 — Trust basis for automatic kills is thin.\n- statement: Auto-kill is 'operator-granted' but rests on a one-night corpus and an unverified classifier (F1–F3). No shadow-mode, no kill rate-limit, no human-override path stated.\n- why-it-matters: A wrong classifier with kill authority destroys work irreversibly; at scale a single parser bug could nuke a whole swarm. Trust basis must be: demonstrated precision on labeled corpus + shadow burn-in + per-window kill cap (e.g., <=1 kill/10min) + always-available manual disable.\n- cheapest-test: Mandate shadow-mode phase (emit WOULD-KILL+evidence, no kill) for a defined period; require zero false positives on labeled data; then enable kills behind a rate cap + global kill-disable switch.\n- severity: MUST FIX (blocking for the auto-kill grant).","created_at":"2026-08-24T01:50:42.036432403Z","kind":"observation","signed_by":"SHA256:usl0k0EVKIRzWIYxQlgcjiM/cGQ8uEjxBXwkMq/YBro","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgCLvCYlub0EX1P/3vBtfMaCQEYV65ygOLwZSOiPTrhK4AAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABAQWw5yteU9MmlkWMmPciS09b49nEdLVWLixrz+GT+eJ6hYtV0Dcg/7b3fMSmQjJWk1W82t2OWOzZD8kAEytjPDg=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:usl0k0EVKIRzWIYxQlgcjiM/cGQ8uEjxBXwkMq/YBro","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgCLvCYlub0EX1P/3vBtfMaCQEYV65ygOLwZSOiPTrhK4AAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQLhMGovpBYYSpSSEDBWdCYTId0VLasw44h7CNTtYLmJC/h83DFzVoORGdHx8mGqH150vdA0xgciDaQuqSFXCdA8="}
{"agent_id":"pp3g-4eBL-clean-room-adversarial-review-on-444-you-are-one-of","agent_seq":5,"timestamp":"2026-08-24T01:51:09.489308141Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"36ca7a67-bf3a-41d3-8648-353118bdde58","comment_uuid":"ee26d19e-e57d-48ac-8197-63b83980a4ac","author":"pp3g-4eBL-clean-room-adversarial-review-on-444-you-are-one-of","content":"FINDINGS (3/4) — tail SPOF, persistence, rotation, session-ID, injection\n\nF5 — Tail-process is a single point of failure with no stated supervision.\n- statement: One continuous tail performs all detection. The 'reduced 60s poll backstop' detects watcher death but doesn't perform detection; no restart owner stated.\n- why-it-matters: Current poll is crash-resilient (fresh process each run). Continuous design concentrates capability into one long-lived process with the same death modes it detects (OOM, uncaught parse exception, lost log handle on rotation). If it dies unrestarted, you regress to blind polling with false confidence. The backstop must trigger automatic restart AND the restart must resume from a persisted offset (F6).\n- cheapest-test: Kill the watcher mid-run; verify backstop detects within 60s, an external supervisor restarts it, and it resumes without re-firing or missing events.\n- severity: HIGH (must specify supervision + restart semantics).\n\nF6 — No persisted read-position; restart drops or replays events.\n- statement: Proposal doesn't mention persisting tail offset/inode across restarts/rotations.\n- why-it-matters: Naive tail -F restarts at EOF, missing the downtime window (a death during downtime goes undetected until next poll — defeating the mechanism). Restarting from file start replays history and can re-fire kills for resolved agents. Rotation while down loses the old inode.\n- cheapest-test: Simulate watcher crash + rotation during a live run; verify resumed watcher neither misses the gap nor re-fires historical lines (needs inode+offset checkpoint + rotation-recovery path).\n- severity: HIGH (required for event-model correctness).\n\nF7 — Rotation handling hand-waved; copytruncate breaks tail -F.\n- statement: 'tail -F style' handles rename-and-recreate but NOT in-place truncation (logrotate copytruncate), which keeps the inode and can drop/duplicate lines at the boundary.\n- why-it-matters: If deployment uses copytruncate (common default), lines are silently lost or duplicated at rotation => missed detections or spurious re-classifications.\n- cheapest-test: Reproduce the exact rotation method used; verify line delivery across one rotation with a known injected sequence.\n- severity: MEDIUM-HIGH.\n\nF12 — Session-ID lifecycle/reuse can bleed attribution across agents.\n- statement: Agents churn; if the log's session ID is reused after cleanup, a new agent inherits the prior agent's trailing window/state => spurious SPIRAL/STREAM-DEATH. Not addressed.\n- why-it-matters: Attribution state keyed by a reusable ID is a safety hole: a fresh healthy agent could be killed for inheriting a 'spiral' window.\n- cheapest-test: Verify session-ID uniqueness/monotonicity in real logs; if reusable, key watcher state by (session-id + spawn-time) or worktree path and expire on disappearance.\n- severity: MEDIUM-HIGH.\n\nF15 — Log injection/spoofing if agent content shares the log (security).\n- statement: If agent stdout/tool-output is interleaved into the shared log and the parser can't distinguish binary-emitted control lines from agent content, a buggy/adversarial agent could forge 'AI_APICallError' (avoid kill) or spoof another's stream-death.\n- why-it-matters: Classifier trust (F11) assumes a trustworthy log; if attribution tags are influenceable, the safety mechanism is gameable.\n- cheapest-test: Confirm session-ID/control lines are written by the trusted opencode binary (not the agent); if agent content shares the stream, require a structured trusted prefix agents can't emit.\n- severity: MEDIUM (security).","created_at":"2026-08-24T01:51:09.483094520Z","kind":"observation","signed_by":"SHA256:usl0k0EVKIRzWIYxQlgcjiM/cGQ8uEjxBXwkMq/YBro","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgCLvCYlub0EX1P/3vBtfMaCQEYV65ygOLwZSOiPTrhK4AAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABA3nY0YjOm+23UyeswAAv5tkMPXiDC0iHJeGAGMUcI8BTZSe/iH3+M7aZb4P7VCrD/H552yG7Gx23Jysc+gy5MCA=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:usl0k0EVKIRzWIYxQlgcjiM/cGQ8uEjxBXwkMq/YBro","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgCLvCYlub0EX1P/3vBtfMaCQEYV65ygOLwZSOiPTrhK4AAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQOxGqYgr/tUW3ZtQJ3cntZ4kQIx31mW3JTkLZorprITRApeW51H/Xo94uZvcK/cCLz0mcV8wWQOZlkoBMqklZAU="}
{"agent_id":"pp3g-4eBL-clean-room-adversarial-review-on-444-you-are-one-of","agent_seq":6,"timestamp":"2026-08-24T01:51:37.863195461Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"36ca7a67-bf3a-41d3-8648-353118bdde58","comment_uuid":"03806379-67a1-4cc7-89a5-6d8803f4dcb1","author":"pp3g-4eBL-clean-room-adversarial-review-on-444-you-are-one-of","content":"FINDINGS (4/4) — framing, latency, kill safety, evidence, park timeout\n\nF8 — 'Replacing polling' is inaccurate; a poll remains.\n- statement: Framed as replacing periodic polling, yet retains a 'reduced 60s poll as backstop' that still runs agent-liveness.py (walk + tmux/ps per agent).\n- why-it-matters: Eventing augments, not replaces; polling cost/failure modes persist. Framing affects scope and the 'who watches the watcher' analysis (now two watchers + their supervisor).\n- cheapest-test: N/A (clarification). State explicitly this is augmentation; size the 60s poll as a first-class supervised component.\n- severity: NIT/clarification.\n\nF9 — Latency benefit for STREAM-DEATH is overstated.\n- statement: Eventing's speed helps PARKED-RETRYING and SPIRAL, but STREAM-DEATH latency is dominated by the aging threshold, not poll-vs-event (detected at T+epsilon either way; polling adds <=30s).\n- why-it-matters: The core motivation (silent deaths) is addressed by the threshold, not eventing. Overstating the gain can justify premature auto-kill. The real win is classification quality (parked vs dead vs thinking), which depends on F1-F3, not latency.\n- cheapest-test: N/A (analysis). Right-size expectations.\n- severity: MEDIUM (affects rationale).\n\nF10 — Kill interaction with in-flight git ops and existing guards unspecified.\n- statement: Auto-kill = tmux kill-session / process kill. Not addressed: killing mid-commit (git writes gated on active issue but a kill can interrupt a non-atomic write), coordination with crosslink-guard/orchestrator-guard, or whether kill targets the agent process vs whole session.\n- why-it-matters: A kill interrupting a half-written file/commit corrupts agent state — a NEW failure mode introduced by auto-kill. Existing guards prevent unauthorized writes, not unsafe termination; the watcher's kill bypasses human-in-the-loop for the spiral class.\n- cheapest-test: Define kill primitive precisely (SIGTERM agent process, wait, SIGKILL; never blind 'tmux kill-session'); check for '.git/index.lock' / in-progress commit before kill; document crosslink-guard interaction.\n- severity: HIGH (required before auto-kill is safe).\n\nF13 — Evidence-bundle integrity depends entirely on attribution.\n- statement: Alerts attach an 'attributed log tail ~30 lines'; if attribution (F1) is wrong, the evidence misleads operator/auditor.\n- why-it-matters: Audit trail only as trustworthy as attribution; a misattributed bundle confirms a false premise post-hoc.\n- cheapest-test: Same as F1; in shadow mode have a human verify 10 attributed bundles against ground truth.\n- severity: MEDIUM (follows F1).\n\nF14 — PARKED-RETRYING needs a max-park timeout.\n- statement: 'AI_APICallError + future-retry => PARKED-RETRYING do-not-kill' has no upper bound; a persistent auth/config error retrying forever parks indefinitely, consuming a slot, never escalating.\n- why-it-matters: Do-not-kill is right for transient rate-limits, but a misconfigured agent retrying forever is itself a failure needing human attention.\n- cheapest-test: Define max-park duration (e.g., quota-reset window + margin); beyond it, escalate to a flag (not a kill).\n- severity: LOW/NIT.","created_at":"2026-08-24T01:51:37.857528278Z","kind":"observation","signed_by":"SHA256:usl0k0EVKIRzWIYxQlgcjiM/cGQ8uEjxBXwkMq/YBro","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgCLvCYlub0EX1P/3vBtfMaCQEYV65ygOLwZSOiPTrhK4AAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABAlRwCZkASBJlwnKk3+CZPxNePphJQXk0n+DFzg1AIo0+yReu8ECbAjiR1NQ9A+nZvnuAOB5UB8oQNePbdQQFEAQ=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:usl0k0EVKIRzWIYxQlgcjiM/cGQ8uEjxBXwkMq/YBro","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgCLvCYlub0EX1P/3vBtfMaCQEYV65ygOLwZSOiPTrhK4AAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQHNINa9dopJz4Ptr4A2MdEBaoiKJNpsRFKVsbITgbdZWVKW763YLjikTbNVpx0KEkZqtpZOq8hgXF/N7dkhBIwA="}
{"agent_id":"pp3g-4eBL-clean-room-adversarial-review-on-444-you-are-one-of","agent_seq":7,"timestamp":"2026-08-24T01:51:58.135914191Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"36ca7a67-bf3a-41d3-8648-353118bdde58","comment_uuid":"ae2ae5aa-1f6e-4cad-bf13-f77b5d80e111","author":"pp3g-4eBL-clean-room-adversarial-review-on-444-you-are-one-of","content":"VERDICT: MODIFY (do not adopt as specified; build behind mandatory gates).\n\nThe classification taxonomy — PARKED-RETRYING vs STREAM-DEATH vs SPIRAL, with evidence bundles — is a genuine improvement over today's pane-hash heuristics, and event-driven detection is conceptually sound. But the proposal cannot be ADOPTED as written because four load-bearing elements are unproven or unsafe:\n\n1. Attribution (F1) and request-correlation (F2) are the entire mechanism and are admitted-unverified. If a shared log line cannot be reliably mapped to an agent, every classification and every kill is misrouted.\n2. The parser (F3) is built on one night's inferred strings; it will silently miss real failures (false negatives) — the exact deaths it targets.\n3. Spiral auto-kill (F4, F11) grants irreversible authority on an unverified classifier with no shadow-mode, no rate-limit, no override. Asymmetric risk: a false-positive kill destroys uncommitted work; a false-negative is cheaply recovered.\n4. The tail process is an unsupervised SPOF (F5) with no persisted read-position (F6) and unhandled rotation (F7); it can miss the very events it exists to catch.\n\nMANDATORY MODIFICATIONS before build/adoption:\n- M1 (blocking): Prove attribution + request-correlation against real multi-agent logs from BOTH producers (F1,F2). If unprovable, the event mechanism adds nothing over the existing poll for STREAM-DEATH and SPIRAL becomes unsafe => switch to ALTERNATIVE M1-alt: per-agent log files (one log per session) tailed individually, making attribution structural rather than parsed.\n- M2 (blocking): Build the parser against a real error/stream corpus; add an unrecognized-line-rate alert for schema drift (F3).\n- M3 (blocking for auto-kill): Ship in SHADOW mode first (emit WOULD-KILL + evidence, no kill) for a defined burn-in; require ~zero false positives on a labeled corpus of verbose-good vs spiral; only then enable SPIRAL-class auto-kill behind a kill-rate cap (<=1/10min) and a global kill-disable switch (F4,F11).\n- M4: Specify supervision hierarchy + persisted (inode,offset) checkpoint + rotation-recovery (rename AND copytruncate) so restarts neither miss nor replay (F5,F6,F7).\n- M5: Define a safe kill primitive (SIGTERM agent proc, wait, SIGKILL; never blind 'tmux kill-session') that checks for in-progress git locks and documents crosslink-guard interaction (F10).\n- M6: Key watcher state by (session-id + spawn-time) or worktree path; expire on agent disappearance; confirm log control lines are binary-trusted (F12,F15).\n- M7: Add PARKED-RETRYING max-park timeout -> flag (F14); reframe as augmentation not replacement (F8,F9).\n\nALTERNATIVE-MECHANISM (if M1 attribution fails): per-agent log tails. Each agent/session writes its own log; the watcher tails one file per agent. Attribution becomes structural (the file IS the agent), eliminating F1/F2/F12/F15 entirely. Cost: N file handles instead of one, and requires the fork/TUI to support per-session log paths — but it removes the hardest unsolved problem (parsing a shared multiplexed stream). Recommend evaluating this as the primary design if shared-log attribution cannot be proven cheaply.\n\nNet: MODIFY — the architecture is worth building, but only behind M1-M7. Granting auto-kill before M1-M3 is rejected.","created_at":"2026-08-24T01:51:58.129721587Z","kind":"result","signed_by":"SHA256:usl0k0EVKIRzWIYxQlgcjiM/cGQ8uEjxBXwkMq/YBro","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgCLvCYlub0EX1P/3vBtfMaCQEYV65ygOLwZSOiPTrhK4AAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABAd8RFVq/eNUSu6rIiFqSTl37wKYajwg6/L9Wa